{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You came in with abdominal pain and vomiting after an abdominal massage?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it was sudden—projectile vomiting. I’ve had this before, but it scared me this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Your vitals show a fast heart rate and slightly high blood pressure, which makes sense with pain. We’ve placed an NG tube to help decompress your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I actually placed it myself in the ER. It brought up about 250 cc. Does that mean it’s working?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:05:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s a good sign. It means we’re draining fluid and air. We’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now and give fluids through your IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But I’m worried—could this be another bowel obstruction?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s our main concern. We did a KUB X-ray, and it shows dilated bowel loops, but no clear signs of a mechanical blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:08:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not blocked? But why am I so bloated and in pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of Crohn’s and pseudoobstruction, this looks more like your gut isn’t moving properly—what we call an ileus or pseudoobstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:10:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like last time? I was just here a week ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’re watching you closely. Surgery and GI have been consulted, and they agree with this approach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:12:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying to reduce my Dilaudid at home. I don’t want to rely on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-11-22 21:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. We’ll manage your pain with IV Dilaudid and Valium, as you’ve had before, but we’ll keep it as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-11-23 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I reviewed your labs. Your kidney function was a bit off on admission—creatinine was 1.2—but it’s improved to 0.9 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-11-23 06:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that because I was dehydrated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-11-23 06:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely pre-renal. IV fluids are helping. Your hemoglobin is low at 9.3, but it’s stable—consistent with your known iron deficiency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-11-23 06:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my white count? I’ve had low counts before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-11-23 06:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s 4.4 now—was lower last night. Hematology has seen you before and says this can happen during hospital stays and isn’t always a concern."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-11-23 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your CT scan results. No sign of small bowel obstruction. Your colon is dilated, but there’s no transition point—so likely pseudoobstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-11-23 08:46:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the NG tube? Is it in the right place?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-11-23 08:47:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s in the distal esophagus, not the stomach. We need to reposition it so it can drain better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-11-23 08:48:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can we do that now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-11-23 08:49:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the nurse will help adjust it. We’ll confirm with an X-ray."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-11-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We tried to place a PICC line yesterday for better IV access, but we couldn’t advance the wire due to vein blockages."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-11-24 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Because of my SVC issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-11-24 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. So we placed a midline in your left arm instead. It’s shorter but should work for fluids and meds during this stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-11-25 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest X-ray shows the NG tube is still not quite in the stomach. The side port is at the GE junction. We may need to reposition it again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-11-25 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It’s frustrating. Why won’t it stay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-11-25 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your anatomy is complex from surgeries. We’ll keep adjusting until it’s right. The good news is your bowels are starting to decompress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-11-25 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having some diarrhea this morning—normal for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-11-25 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s actually a good sign. It means your gut is starting to move again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-11-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray shows slight improvement—less distension in your colon. We’re heading in the right direction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-11-26 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try sipping water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-11-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We need to see more bowel activity. We’ll try an enema today to help stimulate movement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-11-27 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great news—you passed stool after the enema yesterday. That’s a big step forward."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-11-27 07:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a bit better. Can we remove the NG tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-11-27 07:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check an X-ray first. If your stomach stays decompressed, we can consider removing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-11-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The X-ray shows the NG tube is now in the stomach. But since you’re improving, we’re going to try removing it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-11-27 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I hate having it in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-11-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well overnight—no nausea or vomiting. We’re going to start you on clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-11-28 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I have broth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-11-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start with broth and see how you tolerate it. Small sips at first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-11-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve kept down clear liquids. Today, we’ll advance you to a soft diet—mashed potatoes, applesauce, things like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-11-29 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m really hungry. Can I have more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-11-29 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We have to be cautious. Your gut is still recovering. Let’s see how you do today, then maybe more tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-11-30 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve tolerated the soft diet well. No vomiting. Your labs are stable. We’re making good progress."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-11-30 07:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-11-30 07:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep this up, likely in a few days. We want to make sure you can eat and keep food down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-12-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back negative—no infection. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-12-01 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a low-grade fever the other night. Was that just from stress?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-12-01 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Your chest X-ray showed a chronic opacity in your right lung, but no new pneumonia. It’s likely stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-12-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The NG tube was replaced yesterday because it got dislodged, but we’ve removed it again today since you’re doing so well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-12-02 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t even notice. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-12-03 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been on a regular diet since yesterday—how’s your stomach feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-12-03 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. No pain, no vomiting. Just mild bloating, but that’s normal for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-12-03 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow if all goes well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made it through the night with no issues. We’ll get your discharge papers ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No changes to my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No changes. You’ll continue your usual medications, including Flagyl as you’ve restarted."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:03:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if this happens again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have severe pain, vomiting, or can’t keep liquids down, come back to the ER. Otherwise, follow up with your GI doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m really glad to be going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-12-04 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Take it easy, stick to soft foods for a few days, and call if anything worries you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-12-05 00:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your discharge orders are in. You’re cleared to go home this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-12-05 00:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-12-05 00:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember—follow up with your PCP and GI team. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-12-05 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in before you leave. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2184-12-05 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I’m good. I’ll follow the instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2184-12-05 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll see you in clinic if needed. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2184-12-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m all packed. Just waiting on the ride."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2184-12-05 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. I’ll sign your discharge papers. You’re officially going home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2184-12-05 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you again. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2184-12-05 10:03:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2184-12-05 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m heading out now. Bye!"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2184-12-05 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Bye! Feel better soon."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-11-22 21:01:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-12-05 12:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 54-year-old woman with a history of Crohn’s disease, short bowel syndrome, and multiple prior abdominal surgeries was admitted for acute abdominal pain and projectile vomiting following an abdominal massage. She was recently hospitalized for similar symptoms attributed to pseudoobstruction. On admission, she was in distress with tachycardia and abdominal distension. An NG tube was placed, revealing dilated bowel loops on imaging, but CT scan showed no mechanical obstruction, supporting a diagnosis of pseudoobstruction. She was managed with NPO status, IV fluids, pain control, and serial monitoring. Her renal function improved with hydration, and after two enemas, she passed stool and gradually advanced to a regular diet. The NG tube was repositioned multiple times before being removed. She remained stable, with no medication changes, and was discharged home in good condition able to tolerate oral intake without pain or vomiting.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Other and unspecified postsurgical nonabsorption",
      "Hypopotassemia",
      "Regional enteritis of unspecified site",
      "Abdominal pain, generalized",
      "Dyspepsia and other specified disorders of function of stomach",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified",
      "Leukocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Other diseases of lung, not elsewhere classified"
    ]
  }
}
